Package Mini Project 1 as a Helm Chart
Instead of managing 5 individual YAML manifests (01-config.yaml, 02-redis.yaml, 03-frontend.yaml, 04-ingress.yaml, 
05-hpa.yaml), Helm combines them into a reusable package governed by a single values.yaml file.

1. Initialize the Chart Structure

helm create k8s-mini-project-1

This generates a template tree:

k8s-mini-project-1/
├── Chart.yaml          # Metadata (name, version, appVersion)
├── values.yaml         # Default configuration values
└── templates/          # Jinja/Go-templated Kubernetes manifests
    ├── deployment.yaml
    ├── service.yaml
    ├── ingress.yaml
    ├── hpa.yaml
    ├── NOTES.txt
    └── _helpers.tpl

2. Clean up Defaults and Add Components

You replace the boilerplates with parameterized templates for:

templates/redis-statefulset.yaml & templates/redis-service.yaml

templates/frontend-deployment.yaml & templates/frontend-service.yaml

templates/ingress.yaml

templates/hpa.yaml

templates/configmap.yaml & templates/secret.yaml

3. Parameterize in values.yaml

Centralize replica counts, image tags, domains, and resources:

frontend:
  replicaCount: 2
  image:
    repository: ghcr.io/stefanprodan/podinfo
    tag: 6.5.4
  resources:
    limits:
      cpu: 150m
      memory: 64Mi
    requests:
      cpu: 50m
      memory: 32Mi

redis:
  storage: 1Gi
  image:
    repository: redis
    tag: 7-alpine

ingress:
  enabled: true
  host: myapp.local

autoscaling:
  enabled: true
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 6
  targetCPUUtilizationPercentage: 50